// What the lane's narrow partition stores and what it delivers, per
// multiply-add route. Measured on each piece's own grid against the
// lane's reference, in binary32 on the coefficients as stored, under
// both schemes the lane's entries sum by - which is the arithmetic the
// entries run and not the binary64 sweep the pieces were placed by. A
// swept maximum on a finite grid: the bar is kRegionAFitBar and, for
// region B, kRegionBFitBar.
struct NarrowRowF32 {
    int scheme, deg, pieces, stored;
    double fused, separate;
};

